Senior Software Engineering Manager (Global Billing, Payments & API ) &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Job title: Senior Software Engineering Manager (Global Billing, Payments &amp;amp; API)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: London / Bristol / Edinburgh (Hybrid Office - 3+ days per week)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary: £100,000 - £125,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team: Global Billing, Payments &amp;amp; API)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Level: PL2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in London, Bristol or Edinburgh and requires existing right to work in the UK.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At this time, we are not able to offer visa sponsorship for this role. We are committed to building a diverse, global team and our sponsorship policy is evaluated on a role-by-role basis. We encourage you to keep an eye on our careers site to stay informed about future opportunities where we are able to offer visa sponsorship.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kaluza.com/&quot;&gt;Kaluza&lt;/a&gt; is the Energy Intelligence Platform, turning energy complexity into seamless coordination. We help energy companies overcome today’s challenges while accelerating the shift to a clean, electrified future.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our platform orchestrates millions of real-time decisions across homes, devices, markets and grids. By combining predictive algorithms with human-centred design, Kaluza makes clean energy dependable, affordable and adaptive to everyday life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With teams across Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, and a joint venture with Mitsubishi Corporation in Japan, we power leading companies including OVO, AGL and ENGIE, as well as innovators like Volvo and Volkswagen.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will I be doing?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Kaluza runs the billing and payments engine behind some of the world&#39;s biggest energy retailers. Every bill sent and every payment collected across Kaluza&#39;s markets increasingly runs through one shared core platform, and GBPA exists to build and run that core, so foundational billing and payments capability gets built once and reused everywhere, rather than rebuilt separately for every new market or client relationship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That matters because of where Kaluza is headed: as we grow into new markets and take on more of the world&#39;s largest energy retailers as clients, rebuilding core billing and payments capability separately for each one is slower, costlier, and more error-prone than building it once and configuring it at the edge. Getting this right directly shapes how fast Kaluza can bring new markets and clients onto the platform, and how reliable that platform is once they&#39;re on it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re also in the middle of reorganising how this part of the business works, moving from building billing and payments capability separately per area toward one shared global core that every area configures rather than rebuilds. Senior Engineering Managers across GBPA sit at the centre of that shift, each owning two domains rather than a single team. Responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll lead engineering across two GBPA domains through complex, ambiguous, cross-squad initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll own technical and product strategy across both domains simultaneously, rather than handing strategy off to a single team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll diagnose systemic and organisational issues using deep domain knowledge, not just resolve team-level technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll manage cross-functional stakeholders across Product, Delivery, and adjacent engineering teams to align roadmap and trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll carry full people-leader ownership for both teams: goal-setting, performance and pay conversations, hiring and recruitment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll operate in a high-integrity data domain (billing and payments) where reliability and reconciliation come before speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ideally you’ll have/be&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a proven track record leading engineering team(s) through complex, ambiguous, cross-squad initiatives — not single-team delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience owning technical and product strategy across multiple domains or services simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a track record of diagnosing systemic or organisational issues and resolving them with deep domain knowledge, not just fixing team-level technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a strong cross-functional stakeholder manager, working with Product, Delivery, and adjacent engineering teams to align roadmap and trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have full people-leader experience: goal-setting, performance and pay conversations, hiring and recruitment for the team(s) you lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be comfortable operating in a high-integrity data domain (billing or payments), where quality and reconciliation matter as much as delivery speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a demonstrable record of applying AI/LLMs to deliver customer impact, not just adopting AI tooling internally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have demonstrable customer obsession and a working-backwards practice: start from the customer problem and ship the simplest solution that solves it, rather than the most sophisticated one available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a track record of successfully navigating complex stakeholder and leadership dynamics, influencing the wider organisation beyond your direct scope to improve product quality and team experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What will set you apart&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience in billing, payments, or API platform domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating a &quot;global core, configurable edge&quot; or multi-market platform model (one engine, configuration at the edge, no client-specific forks of core logic).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring senior engineers toward people-leadership roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you&#39;ll work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We offer flexible working, with an expectation of 3 days a week in the office. This gives us the best of both: real time together to collaborate and build relationships, with the flexibility to work in the way that suits you best the rest of the week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kaluza Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Here at Kaluza we have five core values that guide us as a business: Play to win, Solve the real problem, Build trust every day, Own the outcome, Go further together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discretionary Bonus Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical Insurance + Virtual GP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to Furthr - a Climate Action app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free Mortgage Advice and Eye Tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perks at Work - access to thousands of retail discounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5% Flex Fund - to spend on the benefits you want most&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;26 days holiday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progressive Leave Policy - With no qualifying service periods, including 26 weeks full pay if you have a new addition to your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal Learning Budget - Upskill, learn and grow!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home Office Budget&lt;br&gt;And more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We want the best people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We’re keen to meet people from all walks of life — our view is that the more inclusive we are, the better our work will be. We want to build teams which represent a variety of experiences, perspectives and skills, and we recognise talent on the basis of merit and potential.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We understand some people may not apply for jobs unless they tick every box. But if you&#39;re excited about joining us and think you have some of what we&#39;re looking for, even if you&#39;re not 100% sure, we&#39;d still love to hear from you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Find out more about working in&lt;a href=&quot;http://kaluza.com/&quot;&gt; Kaluza&lt;/a&gt; on our&lt;a href=&quot;https://kaluza-dev.webflow.io/careers&quot;&gt; careers page&lt;/a&gt; and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/kaluza/&quot;&gt; LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Engineering  Bristol; Edinburgh; London

Director, Quality & Release Engineering &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Job title: Director, Quality &amp;amp; Release Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: London or Bristol (Hybrid Office - 3+ days per week)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary: £150,000 - £180,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team: Quality &amp;amp; Release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Level: Director&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in London or Bristol and requires existing right to work in the UK.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At this time, we are not able to offer visa sponsorship for this role. We are committed to building a diverse, global team and our sponsorship policy is evaluated on a role-by-role basis. We encourage you to keep an eye on our careers site to stay informed about future opportunities where we are able to offer visa sponsorship.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kaluza.com/&quot;&gt;Kaluza&lt;/a&gt; is the Energy Intelligence Platform, turning energy complexity into seamless coordination. We help energy companies overcome today’s challenges while accelerating the shift to a clean, electrified future.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our platform orchestrates millions of real-time decisions across homes, devices, markets and grids. By combining predictive algorithms with human-centred design, Kaluza makes clean energy dependable, affordable and adaptive to everyday life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With teams across Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, and a joint venture with Mitsubishi Corporation in Japan, we power leading companies including OVO, AGL and ENGIE, as well as innovators like Volvo and Volkswagen.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will I be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The quality engineering function is shifting&amp;nbsp; from manual oversight and process governance toward an AI-assisted product development lifecycle where QA leads its own domain test strategy and bespoke tooling drives automation maturity.&amp;nbsp; This role will drive this shift in our organization and ways of working.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own quality and release governance at programme level, directly manage an engineering team building AI-assisted automation and test data capability, and set the standard that QA leads across delivery streams work to. You will be as comfortable driving change as you are accountable for outcomes. Responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Quality Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve the quality strategy across delivery streams, aligned to programme objectives and client SLAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain release governance frameworks — release readiness criteria, risk acceptance, and sign-off authorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set quality standards and coverage expectations; ensure QA leads translate these into domain-level test strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive defect governance at programme level — internal and client-facing SLA compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent quality and risk in senior leadership, architecture, and product forums&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Driven Tooling &amp;amp; Automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage a team of engineers building and maintaining bespoke automation tooling, leveraging AI and LLM capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the test data management strategy — including AI-assisted synthetic data generation and environment data integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and select off-the-shelf AI testing tools; define governance frameworks for their use and validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure governance gates are maintained as AI participation in the PDLC grows — accountable humans must remain in the loop for risk acceptance and production judgement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish tooling standards that QA leads can adopt across domains without creating dependency on a central bottleneck&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QA Function Leadership &amp;amp; Operating Model&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop, and performance-manage QA leads embedded across domains; define the operating model and career framework for the function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the accountability split clearly: QA leads own test strategy and tooling choices for their domain; this role owns the standard they work to&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive consistency across streams without becoming a handoff point — enable QA leads to move fast within well-defined guardrails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a quality engineering culture — not a bug-finding one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change Management &amp;amp; Adoption&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the transformation of QA practice from script maintenance to intelligent, risk-based, AI-assisted quality engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive upskilling across the function — building capability in AI tooling, context engineering, and agent-assisted workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage resistance and build confidence in new ways of working; bring the team through change without losing them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate quality outcomes in business terms to senior stakeholders — escaped defect rates, release stability, risk posture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the release quality process end-to-end: environment strategy, regression coverage, go/no-go decisions, and post-release monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed shift-left practices — quality gates early in the PDLC, not just at release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the tension between delivery velocity and release stability, particularly as AI-generated code volumes increase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ideally you’ll have/be&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record leading a QA or quality engineering function of significant scale — including embedded domain leads and direct management of practitioners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has directly managed engineers building tooling or automation infrastructure — not just managed QA practitioners executing test plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has delivered a meaningful QA transformation: AI adoption, automation maturity uplift, defect governance overhaul, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has worked in a multi-client or multi-product platform environment, managing quality outcomes across concurrent delivery streams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has owned release governance in a complex, multi-stream delivery context — including go/no-go accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to energy, utilities, billing, or similarly regulated complex domains is a plus — not essential&lt;br&gt;Strong grounding in test strategy, automation frameworks, and CI/CD integration — sufficient to credibly lead engineers building these things&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of LLMs and AI tooling in a QA context: test generation, defect triage, coverage analysis, synthetic test data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understands test data management principles and the challenges of environment data integrity at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to evaluate build vs. buy for tooling; assess AI testing platforms with appropriate scepticism&lt;br&gt;Comfortable setting strategy and being accountable for outcomes — not just owning process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to operate at programme level with senior engineering and product stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in leading distributed, multi-timezone quality functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator — translates quality metrics into business outcomes; can make the case for investment in tooling and governance&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated experience leading practice transformation in an engineering context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to bring people with them through transitions that challenge established ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity; can hold direction steady while the detail is still being worked out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with observability, production monitoring, and shift-right quality practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you&#39;ll work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We offer flexible working, with an expectation of 3 days a week in the office. This gives us the best of both: real time together to collaborate and build relationships, with the flexibility to work in the way that suits you best the rest of the week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kaluza Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Here at Kaluza we have five core values that guide us as a business: Play to win, Solve the real problem, Build trust every day, Own the outcome, Go further together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discretionary Bonus Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical Insurance + Virtual GP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to Furthr - a Climate Action app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free Mortgage Advice and Eye Tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perks at Work - access to thousands of retail discounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5% Flex Fund - to spend on the benefits you want most&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;26 days holiday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progressive Leave Policy - With no qualifying service periods, including 26 weeks full pay if you have a new addition to your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal Learning Budget - Upskill, learn and grow!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home Office Budget&lt;br&gt;And more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We want the best people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We’re keen to meet people from all walks of life — our view is that the more inclusive we are, the better our work will be. We want to build teams which represent a variety of experiences, perspectives and skills, and we recognise talent on the basis of merit and potential.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We understand some people may not apply for jobs unless they tick every box. But if you&#39;re excited about joining us and think you have some of what we&#39;re looking for, even if you&#39;re not 100% sure, we&#39;d still love to hear from you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Find out more about working in&lt;a href=&quot;http://kaluza.com/&quot;&gt; Kaluza&lt;/a&gt; on our&lt;a href=&quot;https://kaluza-dev.webflow.io/careers&quot;&gt; careers page&lt;/a&gt; and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/kaluza/&quot;&gt; LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Engineering  London

Senior Staff Analog Mixed-Signal Design and Modelling Engineer &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; This role is based at our Oxford, England (UK) office, with the option to work a few days a week remotely.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Up to 5%&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Job ID:&lt;/strong&gt; 1765&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Staff Analog Mixed-Signal Design and Verification Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;Cryo-CMOS IC team&lt;/strong&gt; at IonQ Oxford. In this role, you will design analog and mixed-signal blocks from specification through circuit design, simulation, layout, tape-out and silicon validation. You will also own top-level chip integration and modelling as a first-class part of our Cryo-CMOS development flow. In this you will build and maintain the model of the chip that the whole team simulates against, a mixed-abstraction model combining transistor-level circuits with Verilog-A/Verilog-AMS and SystemVerilog real-number behavioural blocks. You will decide which blocks are represented at which level of abstraction, keep the models faithful to the schematics and measured silicon. The full-chip model will then be used to verify the ASICs that control the quantum processor from room temperature down to a few kelvin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll play an important part in shaping the design, modelling and verification methodology, standards and sign-off criteria that support our work in building the world&#39;s most advanced quantum systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this position, you will build and maintain the model of the chip that the whole team simulates against, a mixed-abstraction model combining transistor-level circuits with Verilog-A/Verilog-AMS and SystemVerilog real-number behavioural blocks. These models will be derived form first-principles mathematics and correlated against schematic and measured silicon. You will decide which blocks are represented at which level of abstraction, keep the models faithful to the schematics and measured silicon. The full-chip model will then be used to verify the ASICs that control the quantum processor from room temperature down to a few kelvin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have the opportunity to set the design and modelling standards the programme signs off against, making trusted models to inform tape-out decisions, and raise the design and modelling capability of the engineers around you, contributing directly to the success of IonQ&#39;s quantum computing roadmap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full-chip modelling strategy: model architecture, abstraction levels, accuracy targets and sign-off criteria used across the IC development flow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning analog and mixed-signal blocks (references, DACs, switches, regulators, clock distribution) from specification through schematic design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own top-level integration: define block interfaces and specifications, assemble the top level, and run the full-chip mixed-signal simulations that verify the ASIC Develop Verilog-A and Verilog-AMS models of analog blocks and assemble them into a simulatable full chip&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build real-number models so the full chip runs in digital verification and regression at practical speed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Derive models from mathematics: turn a transfer function, a Z-parameter network description or a MATLAB analysis into robust Verilog-A with well-behaved tolerances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and run model-versus-schematic correlation, keeping models in sync with design releases, and feed measured silicon behaviour, back into the models and the block designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up mixed-signal co-simulation and regression (Cadence AMS Designer, Xcelium with Spectre) Lead block-level design reviews and mentor engineers on circuit design and modelling craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To be successful, you will need deep analog and mixed-signal design and modelling experience, typically 10+ years. You will have designed blocks proven in silicon and models and used in production tape-out flows. You will bring expert transistor-level design of precision analog blocks (references, DACs, regulators, switches, clock distribution) taken through PVT and Monte Carlo, layout and silicon validation, together with expert Verilog-A and Verilog-AMS and strong real-number modelling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’d be a great fit with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multiple tape-outs with responsibility for block design and top-level integration, including silicon bring-up and bench characterisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong mathematical foundations: linear systems, Laplace and z-domain analysis, network (Z-) parameters, noise and non-linearity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in a production Cadence flow: Virtuoso, Spectre, Xcelium and AMS Designer or similar co-simulation environments, including parasitic extraction and post-layout sign-off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SystemVerilog, plus MATLAB or Python/NumPy for analysis and model validation; scripting to automate model generation, checking and regression&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cryogenic, space or other extreme-environment silicon experience will be highly beneficial, especially designing beyond foundry model validity using measured device data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who can design a block to specification and model it at the right fidelity, derive a model from equations and implement it end to end. You should be able to judge what to model and at what abstraction, align designers, verification and systems engineers on what a model does and does not promise, and contribute effectively within a fast-moving, highly technical team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
